title the config read before the room -- %327, and five of seven roster reds closed on the way
prompt Open as HUSH under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- pick up the running thread, and work Pond completing the ai-jail enclosure under the accrete-only gate boundary.
think ListAgents named no reachable agent, and the process table named one anyway. `ps` showed a second standing_equipment_run.sh --hot I had not started, and its parent is a `codex exec` running the DREAM seat prompt in this same checkout. That is REDS %291's exact condition, and ListAgents cannot see it because a Codex session is not a Claude session -- so the charter law wants the process table beside it, not instead of it. The peer is named above, and every path this lap touched is outside Caravan and Tally.
think The cold roster came back guards_run=79 green=72 red=7, tree_moved=no. Reds first is a standfast, so the Pond lap I had prepared waited behind them. Two of the seven shared one root: tools/fixtures/readme_reach_scan.sh found 26 broken living links, and reds_fold_witness.rish reds because its third duty runs that same scan. Twenty-two are glow/README.md pointing at gen/*.glow after the %301 letter fold, four are active-designing pages pointing at yonder/*.md after today's day fold. foundations_link found a twenty-seventh, foundations/20260727-113304_the-merit-ledger.md -> active-designing/yonder/20260727-105555_nibs-over-the-weave.md.
think Every one resolved by the two fold rules as pure functions of the basename -- first letter for a letter-folded room, first eight characters for a day-folded one -- so the repointer only rewrote a link whose computed target already existed on disk. That check is what keeps a repoint from inventing a path: 26 links rewritten, 26 targets verified present first.
think The mechanism of %327, plainly: tools/ag/agent-jail.sh runs `source "$CONF"` on tools/e/enclosure.conf at line 160, and its own state defaults sit thirty-four lines later at 196-205 as CLAUDE_STATE="${CLAUDE_STATE:-$LOOPS/claude}". A conf that assigns CLAUDE_STATE makes that `:-` default dead code. The shipped tools/e/enclosure.conf.example assigned $REPO/.claude-state and $REPO/.cursor-agent-state -- exactly the two paths adopt_state_dir moves into loops/ at 192-194. So the adoption empties the elder, `mkdir -p "$CLAUDE_STATE"` at 309 recreates it, and --rw-map "${CLAUDE_STATE}:${HOST_HOME}/.claude" at 322 binds an empty directory over the agent's HOME.
think The proof is on disk rather than in the reasoning. .claude-state, .cursor-agent-state and .dream-state all carry mtime 2026-08-28 11:40:13, milliseconds apart, which is that one mkdir line running. .claude-state holds 0 files; loops/claude holds 5,229 including .credentials.json. The launcher's own comment two screens above promises that login is done once per pier.
think Both halves of the seam took a fix. The example now comments all three variables out, so the launcher's seated room is the only spelling of the path -- deleting the second spelling is the lesson written as code. prefer_adopted_room in the launcher lets an adopted room outrank a pin holding NO file at all, which is deliberately narrower than "fewer files": a directory somebody is writing to keeps its place, and a directory holding nothing cannot be a destination anyone is using. The swap is announced on stderr, because a silent correction is the same class of quiet as the fault it repairs.
think The control lifts prefer_adopted_room out of tools/ag/agent-jail.sh with sed rather than copying it, so the six HEAL legs prove the code that runs. Losing the source makes the leg refuse instead of guess -- the same discipline qa_report_card.sh keeps when it lifts measure() out of prose_register_scan.sh.
think Two smaller reds closed beside it. tools/fixtures/pin_bound_touch_scan.sh, seated this afternoon, printed `detail_bound=24576` inside its prove-red block while already holding BOUND_READER; it now reads the bound and derives the one-byte-past figure, so declared_ceiling's deciding count fell 2 to 1. And SKILL.md, landed at the root today, was in the tree and not classified by template-manifest.bron, so sow read M1_BAD; it is allowed and scrubbed like its sibling doors, since it names Keaton twice.
think The council rota read N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3633, so row 3 -- Water and Venus, care and flow, whose sense is taste. Its fixed seat is the happy zone and the thin edge, and that page's whole teaching is that a seam needs an explicit boundary carrying a contract, with collaboration checks on the asker's side and contract checks on the answerer's. The conf is the asker and the launcher the answerer, and there was no boundary between them at all -- the conf simply overwrote a default. The cardinal seat added the diagnosis: Conway, one lap down. Two halves of one contract, written by hands that did not talk, in a tree six always-on bodies write into.
obs Two reds are Mind's and were surfaced rather than crossed. declared_ceiling's remaining line is tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh, byte-pinned by SHA-256 in the MIND adaptation receipt. And session-logs/date/20260828/20260828-142844_the-lane-that-admits-its-own-record.kyri is zero bytes, committed empty at 41eaa0adeb; I checked every ref and no tree has ever held its content, so it cannot be recovered and I will not author another body's record. Its index row promises "Mind's two lane grants". empty_document reds until Mind fills it.
obs The host's own tools/e/enclosure.conf still pins both variables. It is gitignored, so it is one machine's file rather than the tree's, and the scan reports it every run without gating -- a guard that reds on somebody else's machine is a guard someone turns off. The heal covers the credential case there already, since .claude-state holds no file; .cursor-agent-state holds two files from the launcher's own one-time host reseed, so cursor keeps a working auth and loses its chats and projects until that one line changes. Surfaced rather than edited: a gitignored per-host config is the operator's.
obs construction/ITINERARY.md now reads 24575 bytes against a bound of 24,576, and construction/REDS.md 24574 against the same -- one byte of headroom on the card and two in the ledger. The previous lap asked whether a one-page card can hold six always-on lanes at six bytes of headroom; the answer measured today is that it holds them at one, and the next row either lap books has nowhere to go until reds_fold.sh's OPEN-row seat is settled. Both are Keaton's word rather than mine.
obs I left agent-jail.sh as bash rather than taking the standing adaptation grant to Rishi in the same lap. An adaptation is its own witnessed round, and a red repair inside the file being adapted would be two keystones in one.
